Method code:

public JsonSchema getOutermostSchema() {
    JsonSchema context = getDynamicScope().getContainingSchema();
    if (null == context) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("Missing a root schema in the dynamic scope.");
    }
    JsonSchema lexicalRoot = context.findLexicalRoot();
    if (lexicalRoot.isDynamicAnchor()) {
        Iterator<Scope> it = this.dynamicScopes.descendingIterator();
        while (it.hasNext()) {
            Scope scope = it.next();
            JsonSchema containingSchema = scope.getContainingSchema();
            if ((null != containingSchema) && containingSchema.isDynamicAnchor()) {
                return containingSchema;
            }
        } 
    }
    return context.findLexicalRoot();
}

Potential exceptions:
- NullPointerException if getDynamicScope() returns null? getDynamicScope() returns a Scope, presumably never null (maybe if deque empty?). dynamicScopes is a Deque initialized empty. getDynamicScope() likely returns dynamicScopes.peekLast()? Not shown. Could be null if no scope. Then calling getContainingSchema() would NPE. But code calls getDynamicScope().getContainingSchema() directly. If getDynamicScope() returns null, NPE. That is an exception scenario not covered.

- NullPointerException if context.findLexicalRoot() returns null? Then lexicalRoot.isDynamicAnchor() would NPE. If findLexicalRoot returns null, NPE.

- NullPointerException if lexicalRoot.isDynamicAnchor() throws NPE because lexicalRoot null.

- Also, if lexicalRoot.isDynamicAnchor() returns true but later iteration returns null containingSchema; code checks null != containingSchema, so fine.

- If lexicalRoot.isDynamicAnchor() true and iteration returns a scope where containingSchema.isDynamicAnchor() throws NPE? isDynamicAnchor method likely safe.

Thus exception scenarios: missing dynamic scope (getDynamicScope() null), missing root schema (containingSchema null already covered), lexicalRoot null.

